Zachary,

If by "moderate" you mean the effect of nodematch on friendship choice 
depends on the blindness attribute -- an interaction effect in statistical 
terms -- it is possible in theory to have such an effect, but one would 
have to write the ergm term to implement it.

Your question also raises another interesting issue.  Since you're working 
with a directed network, it may be that you would be more interested in 
the *difference* rather than the absdiff for some of your variables. 
That, also is possible in theory, but we haven't written the ergm term to 
implement it.

We have a package that helps users write their own ergm terms, and 
training workshop materials up online with instructions.  ... if you're 
feeling frisky :)   The online materials can be found here:

https://statnet.csde.washington.edu/trac/wiki/Sunbelt2013

https://www.jstatsoft.org/article/view/v052i02

best,
Martina

