HI,
I am running a model which describes the contacts that occur between horses on a farm. I have various descriptors such as the pasture that the horse used, the horse's age ,sex, breed etc. and have formulated a model that looks like this:
m1=ergm(new1~edges +
          nodematch('pasture')+nodematch('breed')+nodematch('use')+
          nodecov('age')+
          nodefactor('pasture')+nodefactor('breed')+nodefactor('use')+gwesp(1))
The model does an OK job at fitting the data, however, when I look at the results summary, I get the following output. I have no missing data, so I'm unsure why I am getting an NA in the nodematch.pasture row.

Iterations:  4 out of 20

Monte Carlo MLE Results:
